  "question": {
    "text": "Let the equations of two sides of a triangle be <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the orthocenter of this triangle is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> then the equation of it&#39;s third side is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>122</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>26</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1675</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>26</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>122</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1675</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>26</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>61</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1675</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>122</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>26</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1675</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
